.TH ARKX 1 "September 2026" "arkx 1.6.3" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
arkx \- fast multi-threaded archive manager (CLI + GTK4 GUI)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B arkx
[\fICOMMAND\fR] [\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B arkx
is an archive manager for Linux with a GTK4/libadwaita GUI and a
command-line interface. It reads most common formats (ZIP, 7Z, RAR,
TAR and TAR.\fIext\fR variants, ISO, CAB, CPIO and more) and writes
ZIP, 7Z and TAR.\fIext\fR archives. Backends: 7-Zip, libarchive and
the Rust native codec, dispatched automatically per format.
.PP
With no arguments it launches the GUI; with a single archive argument
it launches the GUI with that archive open.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.BR l ", " list " " \fIarchive\fR
List the contents of
.IR archive .
.TP
.BR x ", " extract " " \fIarchive\fR [\fIdest\fR]
Extract
.I archive
into
.I dest
(default: the current directory). Supported options:
.RS
.TP
.B \-\-extract-here
Extract next to each archive (file-manager mode). Alias of
.BR \-\-here .
.TP
.B \-\-extract-to \fIdir\fR
Explicit extraction destination. Alias of the positional
.IR dest .
.TP
.B \-\-dialog
Ask for the destination with a native dialog.
.TP
.BR \-p " " \fIpassword\fR
Password for encrypted archives.
.RE
.TP
.BR a ", " create " " \fIdest\fR \fIfile\fR...
Create an archive; the format is inferred from the extension of
.IR dest .
.RS
.TP
.BR \-l " " \fI0\-9\fR
Compression level (default: the active GUI profile).
.TP
.BR \-p " " \fIpassword\fR
Encrypt with a password (AES-256 for 7z/zip).
.TP
.BR \-v " " \fIsize\fR
Split into volumes (.7z/.zip/.rar); size examples: 50m, 1g, 1000000.
.I zip
and
.I rar
need Info-ZIP `zip` / `rar` installed.
.RE
.TP
.BR u ", " add " " \fIarchive\fR \fIfile\fR...
Add files to an existing archive (zip/7z/tar).
.RS
.TP
.BR \-\-to " " \fIdir\fR
Entry paths relative to
.I dir
(default: the archive root).
.TP
.BR \-p " " \fIpassword\fR
Password for encrypted 7z/zip.
.TP
.BR \-\-threads " " \fIN\fR
Cap worker threads.
.RE
.TP
.BR r ", " remove ", " rm " " \fIarchive\fR \fIentry\fR...
Delete entries from an archive (zip/7z/tar).
.TP
.BR mk ", " mkdir " " \fIarchive\fR \fIfolder\fR " " [\fI\-p\fR \fIpassword\fR]
Create an empty folder inside the archive.
.TP
.BR rn ", " rename " " \fIarchive\fR \fIold\fR \fInew\fR " " [\fI\-p\fR \fIpassword\fR]
Rename an entry inside the archive.
.TP
.BR t ", " test " " \fIarchive\fR [\fIentries\fR...] [\fI\-p\fR \fIpassword\fR]
Test archive integrity; prints a per-entry pass/fail report and returns a
non-zero status if any entry failed.
.TP
.BR o ", " open " " \fIarchive\fR \fIentry\fR " " [\fI\-p\fR \fIpassword\fR]
Extract the entry to a temporary location and open it with the default
application.
.TP
.BR w ", " wipe " " \fIarchive\fR \fIentry\fR... " " [\fI\-\-passes\fR \fIN\fR]
Securely overwrite entries inside the archive before removal.
.TP
.BR c ", " compress " " [\fIoptions\fR] \fIfile\fR...
Compress files/folders Dolphin-style; by default creates
.IR name ".\fIfmt\fR"
next to the sources without overwriting.
.RS
.TP
.BR \-\-format " " \fIzip|tar.gz|7z\fR
Target format.
.TP
.BR \-\-to " " \fIdest\fR
Destination archive path.
.TP
.BR \-\-here
Compress next to the sources.
.TP
.BR \-\-dialog
Ask with a native dialog.
.TP
.BR \-\-progress
Show the in-app progress window.
.RE
.TP
.BR convert " " \fIsrc\fR " " \fIdest\fR " " [\fI\-l\fR \fI0\-9\fR] [\fI\-p\fR \fIpassword\fR] [\fI\-\-threads\fR \fIN\fR]
Re-pack one archive into another format (zip/7z/tar.* destinations).
.SS Common flags
.TP
.BR \-p " " \fIpassword\fR
Password for encrypted archives.
.TP
.BR \-\-threads " " \fIN\fR
Cap worker threads (default: auto from CPU/RAM).
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print help and exit.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print version and exit.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B ARKX_THREADS
Number of worker threads to use (same as \fB\-\-threads\fR).
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
Operational error (archive not found, unreadable source, failed operation).
.TP
.B 2
Usage error (invalid or missing arguments, unknown command or flag).
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
arkx l archive.zip
arkx x archive.7z ~/Downloads
arkx x archive.rar . -p secret
arkx extract --here download.zip
arkx a archive.7z file1.txt folder/ -l 9 -p pwd
arkx a movie.7z movie.mkv -v 100m            # split 100MB volumes
arkx add archive.zip backup.txt --to docs/   # add into docs/
arkx remove archive.zip docs/backup.txt      # delete an entry
arkx compress --here --format=zip docs/      # docs.zip next to docs/
arkx compress --dialog photos/               # Compress to... (kdialog)
arkx convert old.rar new.zip                 # re-pack into another format
arkx archive.tar.gz                          # open GUI
.fi
